  "id": "COMPOUND:28880 - PROTEIN:6311",
  "verbalization": "Cytochalasin Z11 is shown to have a target relationship with LoVo, a cancer cell line, through multiple pathways. The evidence suggests that Cytochalasin Z11 acts on LoVo cells, which are targeted by several compounds, including 4-hydroxy-2-[(3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxan-2-yl]oxy-1,4-benzoxazin-3-one and N-[(3S,4R,5R,8S,9S,10R,13S,14S,17S)-17-[(1S)-1-(dimethylamino)ethyl]-4-hydroxy-10,13-dimethyl-2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9,11,12,14,15,16,17-tetradecahydro-1H-cyclopenta[a]phenanthren-3-yl]-3,4-dimethylpent-3-enamide. All of these compounds are linked to Histone deacetylase 5, indicating a potential mechanism of action involving this enzyme. The consistent targeting of LoVo by multiple compounds, all of which are linked to Histone deacetylase 5, suggests a possible role for Histone deacetylase 5 in the biological processes of LoVo cells. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Cytochalasin Z11 and Histone deacetylase 5, though the exact mode of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
